WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.820
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.780
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.820
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:55.200
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:01.950
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:08.290
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.130
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:20.140
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.390
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.390
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:33.480
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.490
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:42.700
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:49.000
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:55.340
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.430
His name is Zero

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.780
<i>A 705 has been reported</i>
<i>at Babylon Construction Block.</i>

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.450
<i>Division 2, mobilize! I repeat...</i>

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.810
Is something wrong, Miss Izumi?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.480
Are you still sleepy?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.950
<i>Why did I dream about that</i>?

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:57.500
It's finally happened.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.340
It's been a long year.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.090
Shige...

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:02.300
Thank you.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.680
Oh, we're just doing our job.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.270
They're back.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.190
Lt. Gomioka,
I leave this in your hands.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:21.240
This will be the last time
we use them.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.080
Lower the deck.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.130
Good morning.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.470
Good morning.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.060
You have my sympathy.
Those early morning jobs are rough.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.810
Now maybe we'll both
get a chance to relax.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.570
What are they going to do
with your Python?

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.320
It'll go to a training center.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.700
I'm glad they can still use it.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:17.710
Well, that sure happened fast.

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:23.010
It was a quick decision,
but wasn't development fast, too?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:28.180
This thing's loaded up with
everything but the kitchen sink.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:35.100
Maybe because they finally
gave up on an economy model.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.020
So now they've gone overboard
in the other direction.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:43.280
You're too loud.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.240
I can't accept this!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.160
There's nothing we can do.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:54.950
The old plan was to simplify
by upgrading both divisions at once.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:59.960
But the new machines cost
a lot more than Ingrams.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.750
I'm not talking about that!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.500
Then what are you talking about?

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.510
I don't care if Division 1
gets an upgrade,

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.260
but why couldn't I help out in the tests?
That's the problem here!

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:16.020
It's because of the new
computer system they're using.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:17.940
New system?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.400
A neural network.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.270
What's that?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.400
This Labor has a nervous system.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:28.860
Will it feel pain?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:36.580
I don't understand. How can you
connect nerves to a machine?

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:41.000
Does it help if you picture
the computer as the "brain?"

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:46.880
But a computer is more precise
than a human brain.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.720
Why go back to nerves?

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.260
There are advantages
and disadvantages.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:58.180
For example, dogs and cats walk
by alternating left and right legs.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.480
But when running, they alternate
front and back legs.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:02.350
So?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.570
A computer is just a big calculator.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.150
It calculates speed, terrain,
the local environment,

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:17.910
and then calculates how to move
the legs. It's extremely complex.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:21.000
But that's what a neural network
excels at!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.000
A neural net machine will have
a lot of advantages.

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.880
Such as?

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:32.800
If the pilot passes out, it could
continue his movement patterns.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.140
The job of piloting
will become far easier.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.180
I don't like the sound of that.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.690
It disturbs me to hear you
say that, sir.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:47.440
Neural networks are vastly easier
to train than simple computers.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:53.160
As mechanics we have to get used
to pushing the envelope.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.330
You're hard at work.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:02.040
Captain, will the new model
arrive on schedule?

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.500
I hope so. It's never wise
to keep the brass waiting.

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:09.460
Come help out in the hangar, later.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:26.810
Ow!

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.730
Are you okay?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.070
I found it!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.820
Oh, nice picture. Is that Alphonse?

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:43.160
I thought I'd lost it,
but it was just behind the drawer.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:47.130
I told you that you should
have cleaned up earlier.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:52.880
Oh, how cute! So is your Ingram
"Alphonse the Second?"

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.720
No, the third. This was the first,
and then I had a cat.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.600
There's a picture of him
around somewhere, too.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.600
The new model's here!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:17.570
Thank you. Go ahead
and take the old machines.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:26.830
Deck up.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.270
Wow.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.280
Well?

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.450
Looks good.

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.410
Want one?

00:09:58.410 --> 00:09:59.660
I don't need it.

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:04.870
Oh, really? Then I guess you
wouldn't mind a practice fight?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.750
With an Ingram?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.250
With an Ingram.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.830
What are you up to?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.880
Nothing.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.040
Okay.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:29.390
Officer Ota, would you
step over here?

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:47.040
Oh, wise Amaterasu,
we humbly beseech you,

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:52.920
on behalf of Special Vehicles,
Second Section,

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:59.260
Division 1 of
the Metropolitan Police,

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:03.760
please grant us your great wisdom,

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:11.770
and guidance in this new endeavor...

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:19.440
Begin.

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.300
Come at me.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.310
It sure does move smoothly.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.560
But Ota's giving him some trouble.
It isn't over yet.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:09.240
That's odd.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:11.750
So, you noticed?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.420
Well, uh...

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:14.540
What?

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.960
Take a look at his feet.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:21.920
He's avoiding the oil drums.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:22.840
What?

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:30.140
Imagine that we're in the city,
and that's construction debris.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:36.860
Lt. Gomioka is deliberately
making this into a real test.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.860
But...

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.780
I've got you on the defensive!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:56.250
That's enough.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.620
Would you like to take it out
for a spin, Captain?

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.420
How does it compare
to the Python?

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:41.840
Operating it makes me tense.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.470
It moves so easily but I have
to carefully consider every move.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:54.720
It could become an icon of safety
or another symbol of destruction.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:58.020
It depends entirely on
the movements I'm training into it.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:05.780
I'd like its highest priority to be
the safety of the public.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.030
I think this machine
can achieve that.

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:10.660
Yes.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:20.540
Naturally the latest model
is superior. It's only logical.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.800
Yeah, but how reliable is it?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:31.760
How will its neural network respond
in the heat of battle?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.810
Its other computers are on par
with the Ingram's.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.440
That's good to know.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.560
Why didn't they just get Ingrams?

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:42.980
Now come on...

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.190
These new machines
are much more expensive,

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.950
so why didn't they just get Ingrams?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.240
Everyone's been coming out
with better models this year.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.450
You know, some day,
even the Ingram may be...

00:14:56.750 --> 00:15:00.080
So Special Vehicles always
has to be on the cutting edge?

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.670
If everyone else upgrades,
we have to upgrade, too?

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.130
It's just a vicious circle.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.630
What ever happened
to wisdom and bravery?

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:16.890
Let's not get too carried away.
A Labor is just a tool.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.980
It's only natural to hone it
and fix minor defects.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.150
Defects?

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:24.480
For example, Ota...

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:30.650
Could you pilot an Ingram
like Noa does, if you had her data?

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:35.490
Of course not. An Ingram's data
is specific to each pilot.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.620
It would be very difficult
to pilot with her disk.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:44.920
Yes, unless you used
a pattern extraction filter.

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:49.670
But current filters tend
to blur the data a bit.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:55.600
True. For peak performance
we train machines for a single pilot.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:00.310
For better or for worse,
your Alphonse belongs to you alone.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:09.570
But the Zero naturally
adapts itself to any pilot.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:15.780
Its neural network responds
appropriately to any pilot.

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:19.240
Although that might make it
more difficult to train.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.840
Care to join me?

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:46.900
The drive train looks similar,
but the electronics are beyond me.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.150
I'm obsolete.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.320
Oh, come on!

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:52.940
Mr. Sakaki?

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:56.820
Yes?

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.790
Do you mind if I report a problem?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:08.250
I'm not sure if I can
help you any more.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.180
Well, it looks like it's time to lock up.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:20.260
Get a grip!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.150
Looks like they're already at it.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.950
Please stop them!

00:17:40.530 --> 00:17:44.250
I already had one
workman's comp yesterday!

00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:47.210
The company's going
to take this out of my hide!

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:51.880
I'm desperate! I'll lose my house!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.170
Machine 1, deck up.
Machine 2, block the target.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.300
<i>Let's take them down quickly.</i>

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.310
Attention Labor: Halt.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.020
Halt!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:34.800
<i>What are you doing, Noa</i>?

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:44.470
<i>Your target is moving.</i>
<i>I'm sending you a map.</i>

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:45.390
Roger.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:49.270
Target moving east, to 204.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.020
<i>Roger.</i>

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:02.370
I have to do something.
But what?

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:12.500
There!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.630
Attention shoppers:
Thank you for your patience.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:19.720
This is Special Vehicles,
Second Section,

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.720
requesting that you clear the area.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.060
Halt your Labor and exit peacefully!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:37.030
No!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.300
You know...

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.640
No. If it's about today,
I don't want to hear it.

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:11.350
I've been messing up all day.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:12.730
What do you mean?

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:16.810
It's great that Captain Nagumo
finally got new Labors...

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.900
But why can't I be happy about it?

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.200
There's nothing wrong
with a little rivalry.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.240
It isn't that.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.080
Was it a mistake to train Alphonse?

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.880
I don't believe so.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.040
But...

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:44.550
Believe in yourself.
You've accomplished incredible things.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.640
It isn't like you to be thrown off,
just by seeing the Zero.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:53.020
You don't have to love the Zero.
Alphonse doesn't want that.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.310
That's all I'm trying to say.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.440
Yeah, I guess.

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.780
Asuma, where have you been?

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:10.330
Chief Fukushima is here! It's bad!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.000
What did I do?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.450
Not you. Izumi!

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:17.210
It's the incident in
the parking lot today.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:21.840
That car the Hercules dented
belonged to some VIP.

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.010
So?

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:30.310
The VIP heard about the Zero,
and now he's complaining.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:34.680
Does he think the Zero could have
prevented the dent?

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.440
That's stupid!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:41.520
We wouldn't be in trouble if we'd
kept the Hercules out of the mall.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:45.990
Whatever the reason,
it means trouble.

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.740
It's a big headache for
the Captain and Miss Kumagami.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.370
Shouldn't Ota
share some of the flak?

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:53.620
What?

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:54.620
Yeah, what!

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.830
This is no time to fight!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:00.540
We may be on the verge
of a major reorganization!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:01.920
Has it gone that far?

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:07.510
Noa!

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:24.280
I was worried about Alphonse,
but I only made things worse.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:31.660
Noa, what's wrong? Come on out!

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:32.870
Noa!

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:38.160
No, I want to be with Alphonse!

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:06.110
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:13.870
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.740
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.740 --> 00:23:21.290
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:29.260
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.970
I got it

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:38.520
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.520 --> 00:23:44.400
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.940
One more chance

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:53.570
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:59.500
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:03.580
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:12.970
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:12.970
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:20.140
I'm not abandoning
Alphonse, no way!

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:22.480
Do you think you
can run from this?

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:23.190
But...

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:26.810
But nothing! If you're not here
what will happen to Alphonse?

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:27.150
You completely...

00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:32.570
But, from long before I felt this way.

00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:38.910
Next Episode, suddenly the last round:
Condition Green. Target, locked on!

00:24:38.030 --> 00:24:44.040
Next episode

00:24:38.030 --> 00:24:44.040
Condition Green
